# Models conventions

- Use `[JsonPropertyName("…")]` for external API shapes (Toggl snake_case / Spesnet lowercase field names).
- Local persistence (`AppSettings`, `SyncState`, `MappingsFile`) uses `ConfigService` camelCase serialization — keep property names readable C#.
- `SpesnetReferenceCache` may live inside `AppSettings`; keep `ClientsByProject` keyed by Spesnet project id.
- Per-user sync config lives under `MappingsFile.Users[togglUserId]`.
- Entry mappings are `UserMappings.EntryMappings` (status + Toggl client + project → full Spesnet destination); do not reintroduce separate client/project mapping lists or a selected-clients checklist.
- Do not store secrets in models beyond what `AppSettings` already holds; never add secrets to committed examples.
- Billing settings (`HourlyRate`, `BillingCycleStartDay`, `DailySyncTime`, `BillingReportDirectory`, `InvoiceTemplatePath`, `InvoiceNumber`) live on `AppSettings`. `InvoiceTemplatePath` is only the file copied once into the data directory as `invoice-template.docx`; invoices always use that copy. Do not commit the docx. `InvoiceNumber` is the latest issued number. The daily schedule, `SyncProblem`, and `BillingReportCycleStart` live on `AutoSyncState`. `SyncProblem` stays set until the next successful sync. Which period used which number lives on `InvoiceNumberLedger` (`invoice-numbers.json`), not on `SyncState`.
